**What happened**:
The function `AreLabelsInWhiteList` return `false` when whitelist is empty.
The function is implemented as follows:
https://github.com/kubernetes/apimachinery/blob/829ed199f4e0454344a5bc5ef7859a01ef9b8e22/pkg/labels/labels.go#L146
```golang
func AreLabelsInWhiteList(labels, whitelist Set) bool {
	if len(whitelist) == 0 {
		return true
	}

	for k, v := range labels {
		value, ok := whitelist[k]
		if !ok {
			return false
		}
		if value != v {
			return false
		}
	}
	return true
}
```

**What you expected to happen**:
When the whitelist is empty, any key of labels can not in it. Should the function return `false` when whitelist is empty?
